      \field{abstract}{We prove that every monotone circuit which tests st-connectivity of an undirected graph on n nodes has depth Ω(log2n). This implies a superpolynomial (nΩ(log n)) lower bound on the size of any monotone formula for st-connectivity.The proof draws intuition from a new characterization of circuit depth in terms of communication complexity. It uses counting arguments and Extremal Set Theory.Within the same framework, we also give a very simple and intuitive proof of a depth analogue of a theorem of Krapchenko concerning formula size lower bounds.}
